== Tornado Analysis

Tornado Analysis is a risk analysis tool used to find which factors have the greatest effect on a project result. It can be used to analyze factors such as cost, time, resources, and schedule.
#figure(image("/assets/image-40.png",width:55%),caption: "Tornado Analysis ")

*Why is it called "Tornado"?*

It is called Tornado Analysis because its results are shown in a tornado-shaped diagram. The factors with the greatest impact on the project are shown with longer bars, while factors with less impact are shown with shorter bars. Thus, the diagram looks like a tornado and makes it easy to identify the most important factors affecting the project.

